WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Open a Bible and you
are holding a library:

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:07.860
law, history, poetry, prophecy, letters.

3
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.550
Biblia, in Greek, simply means the books.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.270
They were written over many
centuries by many authors.

5
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.070
Its agreed list of books
is called the canon,

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.630
from a Greek word for a measuring rod.

7
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.270
So if human hands wrote
and chose every book,

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.180
how can Christians call it God's word?

9
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.570
In this mission, you'll map
Christian views of the Bible,

10
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.840
from every word guided by God to a
human record of experiences of God.

11
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.920
Then you'll read what the Bible's own
writers say about where its words came from.

12
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.470
Your mission: find out how Christians
can call the Bible God's word,

13
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.570
though humans wrote and chose it.
